System Users / Actors:
Student
Search equipment, view availability, reserve eligible equipment, cancel eligible reservations, and view personal reservations/checkouts. 
Faculty
Perform user reservation functions; business rules may permit different limits from students. 
Staff / Administrator
Manage equipment records and process equipment checkout and return operations. 


Functional Requirements:
FR-1 User and Role Support 
The system shall distinguish among Student, Faculty, and Staff/Administrator roles. 
FR-2 View User Activity 
A user shall be able to view their current reservations and active checkouts. 
FR-3 Equipment Information 
The system shall maintain equipment information including an identifier, name, type, status, and availability. 
FR-4 Equipment Status 
Equipment shall support at least AVAILABLE, RESERVED, CHECKED_OUT, and MAINTENANCE states. 
FR-5 Equipment Administration 
Authorized staff shall be able to add and update equipment information. 
FR-6 Search Equipment 
A user shall be able to search for equipment and filter results by at least one criterion such as equipment type. 
FR-7 View Availability 
The system shall display whether equipment is available for reservation or checkout. 
FR-8 Create Reservation 
An eligible user shall be able to reserve available equipment. 
FR-9 Prevent Invalid Reservation 
The system shall prevent reservation of equipment that is unavailable or otherwise ineligible for reservation. 
FR-10 Reservation Limits 
The system shall enforce a configurable maximum number of active reservations and/or checkouts for a user role. 
FR-11 Cancel Reservation 
A user shall be able to cancel an eligible reservation. 
FR-12 Checkout Equipment 
Authorized staff shall be able to check out eligible equipment to an eligible user. 
FR-13 Checkout Data 
The system shall record the checkout date and due date. 
FR-14 Return Equipment 
Authorized staff shall be able to process an equipment return. 
FR-15 Availability Update 
The system shall update equipment status/availability when reservation, checkout, return, or maintenance operations occur. 
FR-16 Notification 
The system shall generate a notification when a reservation or checkout is successfully completed. 
FR-17 REST API 
The system shall expose major operations through REST endpoints using appropriate HTTP methods and JSON data. 


Non-Functional Requirements:
NFR-1 Maintainability 
Business rules shall be separated from UI/controller and database-access concerns. 
NFR-2 Testability 
Service-layer business logic shall be testable without requiring a live database. 
NFR-3 Modularity 
Components shall have clear responsibilities and use interfaces at appropriate boundaries. 
NFR-4 Usability 
The user interface or API demonstration shall provide clear success and error feedback. 
NFR-5 Reliability 
Invalid operations shall be rejected without leaving inconsistent reservation, checkout, or equipment state. 
NFR-6 Code Quality 
Code shall use meaningful names, appropriate encapsulation, and consistent formatting. 


User Stories and Acceptance Criteria:
US-1: (FR-1). As a student, I want the system to distinguish my role, so that I can search and reserve equipment, cancel reservations, and view personal reservations and checkouts.
  A student is permitted the roles, operations, limitations allowed for Student, including searching equipment, viewing availability, reserving eligible equipment, canceling eligible reservations, viewing personal reservations.
  The system applies the student limit and loan period.
  The system denies access to administrator operations.
US-2: (FR-1) As a faculty member, I want the system to distinguish my role, so that I can search and reserve equipment, cancel reservations, and view personal reservations and checkouts with different limitations from a student.
  A faculty member is permitted the roles, operations, and limitations allowed for Faculty, including searching equipment, viewing availability, reserving eligible equipment, canceling eligible reservations, viewing personal reservations.
  The system applies the faculty member limit and loan period.
  The system denies access to administrator operations.
US-3: (FR-1) As an administrator, I want the system to distinguish my role, so that I can manage equipment records and process equipment checkout and return operations.
  An administrator is permitted the roles and operations allowed for an Administrator, including managing equipment records, processing equipment checkout, and processing equipment return.
  An administrator is not permitted to create reservations.
US-4: (FR-2) As a user, I want to view my current reservations and active checkouts, so that I know what is currently on hold and when equipment is due.
  The system displays only active reservations and active checkouts.
  The system displays the records of that specific user.
  The system displays the checkout date and due date of the active checkouts.
  The system displays an empty list for reservations if there are no active reservations.
  The system displays an empty list for checkouts if there are no active checkouts.
US-5: (FR-3, FR-4, FR-5) As an administrator, I want to add equipment, so that the equipment can be reserved and checked out.
  An administrator is able to add equipment identifier, name, type, and status.
  The system will accept the added equipment if equipment identifier, name, type, and status are filled out.
  The system only accepts equipment status of AVAILABLE, RESERVED, CHECKED_OUT, or MAINTENANCE.
  The system will not accept the added equipment if a field is missing.
  The system will not accept the equipment if the user is not an administrator.
  The system will not accept the added equipment if there is a duplicate equipment identifier.
US-6: (FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-15) As an administrator, I want to update the equipment information, so that students and faculty can know when the equipment is available, reserved, checked out, or under maintenance.
  An administrator is able to update the equipment status from AVAILABLE to MAINTENANCE.
  An administrator is able to update the equipment status from MAINTENANCE to AVAILABLE.
  An administrator is able to update equipment name and type.
  The system rejects an administrator to update the equipment status to MAINTENANCE if the equipment status is either RESERVED or CHECKED_OUT.
  The system rejects a non-administrator from updating equipment information.
US-7: (FR-6) As a user, I want to search and filter equipment by type, so that I can find what I need.
  A user can apply zero or more filters.
  A user can search for equipment by its name.
  The system displays only the equipment that meets the filter and/or search criteria.
  The system displays all of the equipment if no filter or search criteria are used.
  The system displays an empty equipment list if there are no matches to the filter or search criteria.
US-8: (FR-3, FR-7) As a user, I want to see whether equipment is available, so that I know whether I can reserve the equipment.
  The system displays the current status of the equipment.
  The system displays available equipment as AVAILABLE.
  The system displays reserved equipment as RESERVED.
  The system displays checked out equipment as CHECKED_OUT.
  The system displays equipment under maintenance as MAINTENANCE.
US-9: (FR-8, FR-15) As a user, I want to reserve available equipment, so that I can use it for my classes.
  The system creates an active reservation for the user and equipment with a reservation status of ACTIVE.
  The system updates the equipment status to RESERVED.
  A second user cannot reserve the exact same equipment.
US-10: (FR-9) As a user, I want to receive a clear message when I cannot reserve equipment, so that I know why that is the case.
  The system prevents invalid reservation if the equipment has a status of RESERVED, CHECKED_OUT, or MAINTENANCE.
  The system displays that equipment with status of RESERVED, CHECKED_OUT, or MAINTENANCE cannot be reserved.
  The system does not create a reservation and the equipment status is unchanged.
US-11: (FR-10) As a system administrator, I want to set a maximum limit of active reservations and checkouts for each user role, so that equipment is shared fairly.
  A student is limited to default limits, loaded from configuration, for active reservations and active checkouts at a time.
  A faculty member is limited to default limits, loaded from configuration, for active reservations and active checkouts at a time.
  The system denies a user a reservation if the user reached their maximum limit of active reservations and checkouts.
  The system allows a user a reservation if the number of active reservations and checkouts is below their limit.
  The system allows a Faculty member to have a higher limit of active reservations and checkouts compared to students.
  The system calculates limitations based on the number of active reservations and checkouts; cancelling a reservation or returning equipment clears up space for new reservations or checkouts. Fulfilling a reservation, turns it into an active checkout.
US-12: (FR-11, FR-15) As a user, I want to cancel a reservation, so that other people can reserve and check out the equipment.
  A user is only able to cancel active reservations that belong to them.
  The system cancels the active reservation owned only by that user and updates the equipment status to AVAILABLE and updates the reservation status to CANCELLED.
  The system denies reservation cancellation if the reservation status is CANCELLED or FULFILLED or does not belong to the user.
  The system denies reservation cancellation if the reservation does not exist.
US-13: (FR-12, FR-15) As an administrator, I want to check out equipment to a user, so they can borrow the equipment for their benefit.
  The system allows equipment with status of RESERVED to be checked out only by the user who reserved it and updates the reservation status to FULFILLED.
  The system updates the equipment status to CHECKED_OUT.
  The system updates the checkout status to ACTIVE.
  The system allows equipment with status of AVAILABLE to be checked out by any student or faculty member.
  The system denies equipment to be checked out if the equipment status is CHECKED_OUT, MAINTENANCE, or RESERVED by another user.
  The system denies equipment to be checked out if the user exceeds their limitations.
US-14: (FR-13) As an administrator, I want every checkout to record the current date and determine the due date of the equipment, so that users are aware of when equipment needs to be returned.
  The system records the date of when the checkout took place.
  The system calculates the due date based on the checkout date and loan period for the user role based on configuration.
  The system displays the due date to the user.
US-15: (FR-14, FR-15) As an administrator, I want to process equipment returns, so that equipment becomes available for other users to reserve and checkout.
  The system updates the equipment status to AVAILABLE.
  The system updates the checkout status to RETURNED.
  The system rejects returning equipment that does not have the checkout status of ACTIVE.
  The system records the return date for the equipment.
US-16: (FR-16) As a user, I want to receive a notification when a reservation or checkout is successfully completed, so that I have a confirmation.
  The system displays a successful reservation notification to the user if the reservation was successful.
  The system displays a successful checkout notification to the user if the checkout was successful.
  The system displays no notification if there was a failed reservation or checkout.
US-17: (FR-9, FR-17, NFR-4, NFR-5) As a user, I want invalid operations to leave no inconsistent state, so that data remains clear, consistent, and reliable. 
  The system displays JSON error messages with status and code if there is a business rule violation.
  The system rolls back, if updates or adding new equipment fails.
  The system erases partial changes, if reservation, cancellation, checkouts, or return operations fail.


